[186.183972, "o", "     1\t## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\tThe corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n     6\ttarget the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n     7\tgreatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n     8\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n     9\tapplies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n    10\tboth ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n    11\t\r\n    12\t## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence — field notes\r\n    13\t\r\n    14\tSite visit #195 to corporate accounting captured mailbox exports showing how intercompany netting dispute correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n    15\t\r\n    16\tDuri"]
